 ```
 
+M4 endpoint defaults are now start/max **8000 kbps**. At `--fps=60`, the endpoint defaults to S5 demand pacing: external root BeginFrames on a precise absolute 60 Hz clock, one outstanding tick per root, input ticks at least 4 ms apart, full-pipeline scheduling and `NoCompositorFrameAcks`. It advertises/uses protocol 2 pacing capability with the patched browser. Other FPS values retain the normal clock; explicit external pacing requires 60 fps. `--begin-frame-mode=off|fixed|demand` selects the comparison mode; `--begin-frame-stock-scheduler` suppresses the automatic full-pipeline/ACK flags for diagnostics. The selected policy is retained in `pipeline.capture.pacing`. Shared-fence capture remains the probed default. Results and limits: [S5 pacing](../../research/m4/s5-pacing.md).
+
 Stop the previous test chain first. Set `ENDPOINT_PATH` and `ENDPOINT_ARGS` as for the ordinary control plane, including the Chrome executable and a dedicated browser profile. PowerShell example from the repository root:
 
 ```powershell
